     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "How should filter schedules be discussed for commercial equipment?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Filter intervals follow load, not the calendar. A one inch filter in a hard-working rooftop unit can load up inside a month. A four inch media filter in a quiet office may hold for a season. Kitchens, salons, gyms and print rooms load filters faster than desk space does. A clogged air filter restricts airflow, reducing capacity, freezing coils in summer and tripping limit switches in winter. City & Suburban offers seasonal check-ups. Discuss filter schedules, supply and responsibility between visits in the custom proposal rather than assuming those tasks are included."
